  "id": "0a3b57ca-227f-5b3e-b84b-d5a7dbe53855",
  "slug": "loaded-steak-fries-recipe-7564469",
  "name": "Loaded Steak Fries",
  "recipe_type": "appetizer",
  "brief_description": "Skip going out to the bar, because these loaded steak fries are all you need. Frozen fries are baked, then topped with a homemade cheese sauce, marinated grilled steak, and fresh toppings.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Place beer, Worcestershire sauce, red pepper flakes, and garlic in a resealable plastic bag. Squeeze in lime juice. Add steak, coat with marinade, squeeze out excess air, and seal the bag. Marinate in the refrigerator for at least 2 hours, or overnight."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F (220 degrees C). Spread fries onto a baking sheet and spray with cooking spray."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until crisp, 25 to 30 minutes, or per package instructions."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Meanwhile, make cheese sauce. Melt butter in a saucepan over medium heat; whisk in flour; whisk continuously until mixture turns golden and forms a smooth paste. Pour in half and half and stir until mixture thickens, 3 to 5 minutes. Stir in cheese until melted, 2 to 3 minutes more. Stir garlic powder, oregano, and dill into the sauce."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Meanwhile, preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat and lightly oil the grate. Remove steak from the marinade and shake off excess. Discard remaining marinade. Cook steak on the preheated until firm and reddish-pink and juicy in the center, about 5 minutes per side for medium rare. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read 130 degrees F (54 degrees C). Remove from the grill and let rest for 5 minutes before slicing."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Place French fries evenly on a platter; pour cheese sauce over fries. Top with sliced steak, tomato, red onions, and thinly sliced jalapenos. Serve immediately."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 40,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 15,
